  "admission_and_activation": {
    "activation": "A single serialized graph activation verifies every child is currently BOOTSTRAP_READY and every exact grant is current. Only the committed ACTIVE projection causes workers to release private GO; children then execute the already retained Task without reimport.",
    "capacity": "Admission atomically reserves all N physical slots and all required tag/global allocations or writes none. Worker capacity remains two live children per worker in this slice.",
    "ordering": "Use the approved Flow/authority/graph, sorted-worker, subtask/grant/TaskRun/stream lock prefix. Revalidate capability, liveness and cross-profile occupancy after worker locks.",
    "placement": "Choose online, native-registered workers advertising partitioned-dag-v1 in a versioned supported-profile set. Fixed-P2 and DAG capabilities coexist and share one physical-slot occupancy authority.",
    "race_result": "Concurrent admission, stale capability or partial registration returns a typed refusal and leaves no partial grants, slot rows, tag allocations or activation journal.",
    "ready_barrier": "Each child first performs cap-free same-child code/config preflight and reports CODE_READY. The worker then claims/registers the exact PID/start ticks and supplies the private scoped bootstrap. The child consumes the private bootstrap, reads and validates its authoritative own bootstrap through the preactivation allowlist, retains the exact Task, and reports a second BOOTSTRAP_READY witness. CODE_READY alone never authorizes activation. No routed DATA, user body or signed task event is accepted before every sealed child is BOOTSTRAP_READY.",
    "size": "N equals the sum of sealed operator parallelism and is bounded by the existing graph limit (currently 128). Never hard-code the first fixture count of four."
  },
