  "completion_failure_cancel": {
    "application_failure": "An exhausted physical Task failure marks the graph failed and initiates bounded drain/stop for the remaining branches. Already committed route receipts remain authoritative; no cross-sink rollback or exactly-once external side-effect claim is made.",
    "authority_loss": "Stale Flow holders, stale workers, stale grants and old child capabilities can observe neither new activation nor terminal mutation. Recovery may resume only from persisted graph/control journals and verified current process identity.",
    "cancel": "Active cancel first journals graph cancellation, fences new DATA and replacements, instructs each assigned worker to stop its exact current child, records each stop receipt, releases reservations once, and only then commits Flow/graph cancellation.",
    "cleanup": "Whole-Flow cleanup holds the Flow/graph authority, deletes NI2-011 references, completions/consumers, receipts and payloads in the declared order, and relies on the single deferred input-reference FK only inside that transaction. A partial commit with dangling pins must fail.",
    "normal": "All leaf cursors reach EOF, every physical TaskRun is terminal, every child is reaped/retired and every physical slot is released before the Flow becomes Completed. Logical tag allocation may release at terminal Task state; physical slots release only after exact process death proof."
