  "data_execution": {
    "eof": "A target edge partition becomes EOF only after all sealed contributors are terminal and their accepted routes are committed. Empty targets receive EOF. A failed contributor cannot manufacture COMPLETED.",
    "events": "Pending, Running and terminal TaskRun events are signed by the current scoped child and checked against exact graph, physical subtask, TaskRun, grant epoch and natural key before any coalescing.",
    "failure_finish": "A failed, crashed or cancelled physical Task never uses the success-finish routes and cannot call legacy fail/finish DATA paths. Its signed current-child terminal TaskRun event is the authority. Server event/control integration journals the graph failure and applies the NI2-011 failed-producer transition in the same transaction or a replayable operation bound to that exact accepted event before drain/stop continues. If producer EOF was already committed, the accepted routes remain immutable and the graph still fails; no COMPLETED edge is rewritten or fabricated. The DAG storage adapter overrides and denies the inherited reject_output and fail_task_output legacy hooks; it may only observe or reconcile the exact signed terminal-event result.",
    "finish_routes": [
      "POST /streams/v2/dags/sources/finish",
      "POST /streams/v2/dags/consumers/finish"
