    "operator": "Each operator reads one stable edge-partition cursor. The resolver verifies the REFERENCE envelope and direct same-graph PAYLOAD identity, then returns the original user payload. DAG StreamContext and StreamRunResult use the actual ConsumerBinding.consumer_id (the stable EdgePartition subscriber ID), never TaskRun.id; legacy profiles retain their existing identity rule. The worker never exposes the reference envelope to user code.",
    "replay": "Current authorization is checked before receipt lookup. Lost acknowledgements return the stored route outcome; replacement never recomputes accepted targets. Semantic mismatches conflict without mutation.",
    "source": "A source process emits SourceRecord(position, value). A KeyedStreamOutput may wrap value; position remains the outer source coordinate. The DAG storage adapter submits only the frozen NI2-011 routed source request.",
    "success_finish": "Normal source generator exhaustion calls a dedicated DAG source-finish route with the exact routing context, current SourceBinding and expected accepted position. Normal operator input EOF calls a dedicated DAG consumer-finish route with the exact context and current stable ConsumerBinding. The routed storage adapter overrides close_source and finish_consumer so neither path can fall through to inherited legacy endpoints. These routes are success-only: they revalidate the scoped current child, owner, TaskRun, cursor/position and sealed contributor set, then invoke the NI2-011 producer EOF transaction. They accept no arbitrary error or client-selected targets.",
    "terminal": "YIELD routes one PAYLOAD plus deterministic REFERENCE rows in the NI2-011 atomic transaction. RETURN is state-only and keyless. YIELD(None) is a payload. Input cursor/state advance atomically with routed output and receipt."
  },
